      <h1>Kenya NTSA Services: A Beginner's Guide</h1>
      <p>Learn how to access transport services online, prepare your documents, make payments safely and follow up on your application.</p>
      <a class="button" href="https://serviceportal.ntsa.go.ke/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open NTSA Service Portal</a>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>1. What is NTSA?</h2>
      <p>The National Transport and Safety Authority (NTSA) is the Kenyan government authority responsible for various road transport and safety services.</p>
      <p>Its services include driver testing and licensing, motor vehicle registration, vehicle inspections and transport licensing.</p>
      <p>Official website: <a href="https://ntsa.go.ke/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ntsa.go.ke</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>2. Common NTSA services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Driving licences:</strong> Access the available services for provisional licences, driving licences, renewals and replacements.</li>
        <li><strong>Driving tests:</strong> Check requirements and follow the instructions for booking a driving test.</li>
        <li><strong>Vehicle registration:</strong> Access the applicable registration services for motor vehicles.</li>
        <li><strong>Transfer of ownership:</strong> Follow the official process when buying or selling a vehicle.</li>
        <li><strong>Vehicle records:</strong> Access available vehicle record or logbook services.</li>
        <li><strong>Vehicle inspection:</strong> Check inspection requirements and follow the instructions for your vehicle category.</li>
        <li><strong>Public service and transport licensing:</strong> Check the applicable requirements for the service you need.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not every service has the same requirements. Select your exact service on the official portal before preparing documents or making payment.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>3. What you may need</h2>
      <p>Requirements depend on the service. Before applying, prepare the information relevant to your transaction.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your eCitizen account login details.</li>
        <li>Your national ID details, where required.</li>
        <li>Your vehicle registration number, where relevant.</li>
        <li>Your vehicle logbook or electronic logbook details, where required.</li>
        <li>Relevant buyer or seller information for a vehicle transfer.</li>
        <li>Any supporting documents requested by the portal.</li>
        <li>A valid payment method accepted by the official portal.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Important:</strong> This is a general preparation list, not a universal checklist. For example, a driving licence renewal and a vehicle ownership transfer require different information. Follow the instructions for your specific service.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>4. How to access NTSA services online</h2>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 1: Open the official portal</h3>
        <p>Use the official NTSA Service Portal. Check that the address is correct before signing in or entering personal information.</p>
        <a href="https://serviceportal.ntsa.go.ke/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open NTSA Service Portal ↗</a>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 2: Sign in using your eCitizen account</h3>
        <p>Use your existing eCitizen credentials if requested. If you do not have an account, follow the official account registration instructions.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 3: Select the service you need</h3>
        <p>Choose the correct category, such as driver services or vehicle services. Read the service description carefully before proceeding.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 4: Enter the required details</h3>
        <p>Complete the form accurately. Double-check ID numbers, vehicle registration details and names before submitting.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 5: Attach supporting documents</h3>
        <p>Upload or provide the documents requested by the portal. Make sure scans or photographs are clear and complete, where uploads are accepted.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 6: Review the fee and pay</h3>
        <p>Check the amount displayed for your selected service. Pay only through the payment instructions provided by the official system, then keep your confirmation and reference number.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 7: Follow the next instructions</h3>
        <p>Depending on the service, you may need to book an appointment, attend a driving test or vehicle inspection, or provide original documents. Do not assume that every service is completed entirely online.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h3>Step 8: Track and collect your result</h3>
        <p>Check your application history, account notifications or official status service for updates. Follow the official instructions for downloading, collecting or verifying the resulting document.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>5. Vehicle ownership transfer: important points</h2>
      <p>If you are buying or selling a vehicle, use the official NTSA process for transferring ownership.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Verify the vehicle details and the identity of the parties involved.</li>
        <li>Check the requirements displayed for the ownership transfer service.</li>
        <li>Follow the official steps for the seller and buyer, as applicable.</li>
        <li>Confirm the required payment and retain transaction records.</li>
        <li>Verify that the transfer has been completed and access the relevant vehicle registration record as instructed.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Buyer safety:</strong> Do not rely solely on a screenshot or a seller's verbal assurance. Verify vehicle records through official channels before completing a purchase.
      </div>
      <p>NTSA information: <a href="https://ntsa.go.ke/services" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official list of services</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>6. Fees and processing time</h2>
      <p>NTSA fees and processing times depend on the service and the circumstances of the application.</p>
      <p>Use the amount displayed by the official portal for your specific transaction. Processing may require additional review, an appointment, a test or an inspection.</p>
      <p>Do not rely on old fee lists or promises of guaranteed same-day completion. Keep your payment confirmation and application reference.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>7. Check uncollected documents</h2>
      <p>NTSA provides an official service for checking certain uncollected smart driving licences, number plates and logbooks.</p>
      <a class="button" href="https://servicestatus.ntsa.go.ke/?resource=license" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check NTSA Service Status</a>
      <p class="small">Use only the information requested on the official page and follow its instructions.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>8. Common mistakes to avoid</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Selecting the wrong NTSA service.</li>
        <li>Entering an incorrect ID number or vehicle registration number.</li>
        <li>Uploading incomplete or unclear supporting documents.</li>
        <li>Paying before checking the transaction details.</li>
        <li>Failing to save a receipt, reference number or confirmation message.</li>
        <li>Assuming that payment alone completes a transaction.</li>
        <li>Using unofficial agents who promise guaranteed approvals.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>9. Stay safe online</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access NTSA services through the official NTSA website or its linked service portal.</li>
        <li>Never share your password, one-time password (OTP) or M-Pesa PIN with anyone.</li>
        <li>Do not send sensitive identity or vehicle documents to strangers.</li>
        <li>Verify payment instructions before confirming a transaction.</li>
        <li>Contact NTSA through the official contact details if a payment or application has a problem.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Official contact information: <a href="https://ntsa.go.ke/contact" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NTSA Contact Us</a>.</p>
    </section>

